-- How Idyll is set out: `idyll fmt`, Lingua's `format!` over the grammar
-- (`Syntax`), within 100 columns, a level two spaces.
--
-- Idyll's layout is part of its meaning: a block's items start at its
-- column, a line further right goes on with the line before. So a block's
-- items each start a line of their own, a level in from where the node
-- holding the block began (`Sep`, a layout `;`, breaks the line), and a
-- node broken over lines has what follows its first line further in than
-- it. What formatting changes is the space between tokens, and nothing
-- else: the tokens, comments among them, are the source's, in its order.

use Idyll.Syntax (parseIdyll, formatStyle)

-- `text` set out, or the errors that stop it being read, each with where.
@pub fun formatted (text : String) : String =
  match parseIdyll text with
  | (g, _) -> formatStyle g
